===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}} {{term-label|en|literary}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[wish#Verb|wishing]] of someone a [[smooth#Adjective|smooth]] [[journey#Noun|journey]], or [[success]], especially at a [[parting#Noun|parting]]; {{lb|en|countable}} a [[statement#Noun|statement]] [[express#Verb|expressing]] this.
#* {{RQ:Tyndale NT|book=2 John|verses=10–11|folio=ccc|passage=Yff there come eny vnto you and brynge not this learnynge&#11805; hym receave not to houſſe: nether bid hym '''god ſpede'''. For he that biddeth hym '''God ſpede'''&#11805; is part taker off his evyll dedes.}}
#* {{RQ:Bunyan Pilgrim's Progress|page=18|passage=Then ''Chriſtian'' took his leave of his Friend, and he again bid him '''God ſpeed'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Vanbrugh Relapse|scene=ii|page=90|passage=''Ber''[''inthia'']. Speed her vvell. / ''VVor''[''thy'']. Ay, but there muſt be more than a '''God ſpeed''', or your Charity vvon't be vvorth a farthing.}}
#* {{RQ:Anne Bronte Tenant|volume=I|chapter=The Warnings of Experience|page=279|passage=He never danced himself, and there he sat, poking his head in my face, and impressing all the beholders with the idea that he was a confirmed, acknowledged lover; my aunt looking complacently on, all the time, and wishing him '''God-speed'''.}}
#* {{RQ:James Roderick Hudson|page=28|passage=[I]n the morning, as Rowland at the garden gate was giving his hostess '''Godspeed''' on her way to church, he came striding along the grassy margin of the road and out-whistling the music of the church bells.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Thon|editors=[[w:Jeannette Leonard Gilder|J[eanette] L[eonard]]]; [[w:Joseph Benson Gilder|J[oseph] B[enson] Gilder]]|magazine=[[w:Putnam's Magazine|The Critic: A Literary Weekly, Critical and Eclectic]]|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=The Good Literature Publishing Co.|date=1 November 1884|volume=II|issue=44|page=210|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=9H_mAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA210|column=1|oclc=56697365|passage=Mr. [[w:Charles Crozat Converse|C[harles] C[rozat] Converse]]'s new pronoun [''thon''] of the singular number and common gender has met with a warm welcome from philologists and the press. {{...}} The new word has received a number of '''godspeeds''', some of which we quote.}}
#* {{RQ:Joyce Dubliners|story=A Little Cloud|page=84|passage=Eight years before he had seen his friend off at the North Wall and wished him '''godspeed'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|figuratively}}
## {{lb|en|archaic}} ''Chiefly in'' '''in the Godspeed of''': the most [[important]] [[part#Noun|part]] of something, or [[point#Noun|point]] at which something [[happen]]s; also, the [[last minute]] or [[last#Adjective|last]] [[moment]].
##* {{RQ:De Quevedo L'Estrange Visions|page=247|passage=But a Devil came in juſt in the '''''God-ſpeed''''', and told them; ''Gentlemen Philoſophers'', (ſays he) if you vvould knovv the VVretched'ſt, and moſt contemptible thing in the VVorld; It is an ''Alchymiſt'': {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:L'Estrange Brief History|part=III|chapter=Bedloe and Prance Swore to the Plot as well as to the Murther|page=19|passage=But juſt in the '''''Godſpeed''''', the ''Plot'' vvas ''Diſcover'd''.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Flora Thompson|chapter=‘A Bit of a Tell’|title=[[w:Lark Rise to Candleford|Lark Rise to Candleford: A Trilogy]]|location=London|publisher=w:Penguin Books|year=1941|year_published=1945 (1973 printing)|page=291|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/larkrisetocandle0000thom/page/291/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-14-018850-9|passage=I udn't mind seeing her come in when I was in the '''godspeed''' of washday, and that's saying something.|footer={{small|Originally published in ''{{w|Over to Candleford}}'' (1941).}}}}
## {{lb|en|originally|Ireland}} ''In'' '''[[back of Godspeed]]''': a [[distant]], [[remote#Adjective|remote]], or [[unknown#Adjective|unknown]] [[place#Noun|place]].
##: {{synonyms|en|back of beyond}}
##* {{RQ:Trollope Doctor Thorne|volume=I|chapter=Frank Gresham's First Speech|page=124|passage=If I don't leave you at the back of '''God-speed''' before long, I'll give you the mare and the horse too.}}
##* {{RQ:Shaw Doctor's Dilemma|page=278|passage={{smallcaps|mrs george}}. I have earned the right to speak. I have dared: I have gone through: I have not fallen withered into the fire: I have come at last out beyond, to the back of '''Godspeed'''. / {{smallcaps|the bishop}}. And what do you see there, at the back of '''Godspeed'''?}}

